    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=16$.",
      "worked": "The arguments require $x^3>0$ and $x^2>0$, so the original domain is $x>0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_4(x^5)&=10\\\\x^5&=4^{10}\\\\x&=4^2\\\\x&=16\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $16>0$, the solution satisfies the original domain.",
